# Merge attributes.
#
# `Docs/icecubes-landing-series.tsv` is the tracked, append-only landing series the close gate's
# stall detector reads (see the header of that file). It exists because the merge verdict used to be
# reproducible ONLY from `.claude/claims.md`, which is gitignored on purpose — several lanes append
# to it concurrently, so tracking the prose ledger itself would make every lane conflict on every
# landing.
#
# `merge=union` is what makes tracking the SERIES safe where tracking the prose is not: git's
# built-in union driver keeps both sides' lines when two lanes land in parallel, so an append never
# produces a conflict. It is only ever correct for a file whose lines are independent facts and
# whose ORDER carries no meaning — both true here by construction, and enforced:
# `Scripts/validate-icecubes-close-policy.rb` sorts the series by its recorded UTC stamp rather than
# by file position, refuses two disagreeing lines for one sha (the one shape union merge can hide),
# and refuses a candidate whose series drops or rewrites a line its merge base already carried.
#
# Do NOT extend `merge=union` to a file where a lost or duplicated line changes behaviour — union
# merge resolves by concatenation, never by understanding the content.
Docs/icecubes-landing-series.tsv merge=union
